A directory of markdown imported as one SNGL package: a site.

`import docs "md:./docs/"` makes every `.md` under the directory a page and
every `.sngl` directly in it part of the package, so the `struct Frontmatter`
in `docs/meta.sngl` is the vocabulary each page's frontmatter is checked
against. Each page is a component named for its path, and a page's
subdirectory holds its children: `guide/intro.md` is a child of `guide.md`.

The package hands the program `site`, whose one slot is the layout. It takes
the page as data -- `href`, `frontmatter` and `children` on one `Page` -- and
the page's blocks as a component entry, so the program writes its layout once
and the importer writes one insertion per page. The layout here makes each page
a window and draws the page's children as a list of titles, which is what
`children` is for.

`intro.md` sets no `weight`, and its page shows the declared default. Two pages
each hold a live island declaring `var n`, and they come out as two components
with a cell each, which is the islands counter being the package's rather than
the page's.

deny * `innerHTML` -- a page is a component tree; nothing is handed to a parser at run time

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import docs "md:./docs/"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

docs.site {
    component layout(page, content) {
        ui.window(title=page.frontmatter.title, href=page.href) {
            ui.vbox {
                ui.text(value="weight {page.frontmatter.weight}")
                for var child = page.children {
                    ui.text(value="child: {child.frontmatter.title}")
                }
                content
            }
        }
    }
}
-- docs/meta.sngl --
struct Frontmatter {
    title string = ""
    weight int = 0
}
-- docs/index.md --
---
title: Home
weight: 1
---

# Welcome

The home page.

```sngl mode=island
var n = 1
ui.text(value="home island {n}")
```
-- docs/guide.md --
---
title: Guide
weight: 2
---

# Guide

How to use it.

```sngl mode=island
var n = 2
ui.text(value="guide island {n}")
```
-- docs/guide/intro.md --
---
title: Intro
---

# Intro

Where to start.
